[#:seon.task{:name "collection-marks-slowly-and-records-nothing"
             :intent "`seon.cluster.registry/collect!` (the weekly `seon.maintenance/collect!`) holds Datahike's sweep permit across the whole mark, the reachability extension, two full key listings and the sweep (gc.cljc:128-177); gc-guard admits no :roster or :blob permit meanwhile (gc_guard.cljc:97-106), so every branch! and blob publication waits: 25-28 s at 5 roster branches idle, 82 s under load on pid 66629. The per-test-request collection that ran this after every request is deleted (152ceb62c), so the wait is weekly, not per request. In the fork, mark and list keys before the permit and hold it only to re-mark roster heads and sweep (perf-audit-2026-09-27 item 1 fixes 2-3); drop the inventory's second key listing (registry.clj key-count). An MCP reply whose value is windowed publishes a blob and waits too (a :blob permit waits while a sweep permit is held, proven on a scratch store id): the two 30 s eval_clj timeouts root saw on 2026-09-27, on a 2.5 ms query and on (`seon.cluster.registry/branch-commit-id` nil nil), whose arity refusal answers in 0.44 ms and is windowed, match this class; their collection overlap was not observed (stability-fix-2). The mark half landed in the fork (datahike 25dcaabb)."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.registry/collect! seon.maintenance/collect!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/perf-audit-2026-09-27.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/fix-merge-basis-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/inv-lifecycle-storage-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/storage-gc-runs-without-a-cutoff-so-it-reclaims-almost-nothing.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "root-verification-compares-a-moving-head"
             :intent "branch-reopens? (maintenance.clj ~617) requires the live branch's current head to equal the commit collection-evidence recorded earlier (~602), after a slow digest walk; :cluster-default commits during a collection, so a clean collection can fault 'did not reopen at its recorded commit ID' (a0323a94, 03:06Z 2026-09-27). Inferred from code, not reproduced; a real loss is not ruled out. Verify the recorded commit loads, not that the head did not move. Done when a regression with a write between the evidence read and verification collects clean, and a missing recorded commit still faults."
             :must-read #{seon.maintenance/collect! seon.cluster.registry/branch-commit-id}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/stability-sweep-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-test-request-collects-the-whole-store-under-the-exclusive-gate"
             :intent "`seon.test/run` submits collect-released! after every request (test.clj ~2510-2528): an epoch-cutoff collection that marks every roster branch's whole history (9,168 commits, 202,872 nodes, 25-28 s at 5 branches on pid 75447) and lists all 157,753 store keys twice (4.9 s each; registry.clj ~538 and konserve gc sweep!), to find 537 garbage keys. gc-storage! holds the sweep permit for all of it (datahike gc.cljc:128-177), and gc-guard admits no :roster or :blob permit while a sweep is active or waiting (gc_guard.cljc:97-106), so every branch! (install-gate disposable copy, test world, MCP branch create) and every blob publication waits: pid 66629 saw branch! 82,311 ms, gate-function-install 82,426 ms and with-publication! 34,471 ms behind 82,774 ms collections. Delete the per-request collection (the weekly `seon.maintenance/collect!` remains); in the fork, mark and list before the permit and hold it only for re-marking roster heads and the sweep; drop the inventory's second key listing. Done when a test request submits no collection, and branch! during a collection waits about one second, not the whole mark."
             :must-read #{seon.test/run seon.cluster.registry/collect! seon.cluster.registry/branch! seon.blob/with-publication!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/perf-audit-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-daily-collection-keeps-every-commit-of-a-live-branch"
             :intent "`seon.maintenance/collect!` now applies `seon.cluster.registry/retention-cutoff` (`:seon.config.db/snapshot-window-ms`, shipped as one hour since f048f1251), but no scheduled collection has yet completed on default, so its reclamation is unmeasured. Before that change every commit's rewritten index nodes were permanent: measured 2026-09-28, a commit rewrites 0.3-1.2 MB of nodes, default made 7,646 commits in 24 h, and data/store grew from 102,589,464 to 107,773,192 KB in about ten minutes while this lane's own probe wrote ~40 MB. Owner rule: health and probes must never be a drain, and up to ~1 GB/day is acceptable only if the daily collection reclaims it. Done when the scheduled collection applies a declared snapshot window to live branches (older commits beyond it reclaimed, branch heads and held values kept), with the bytes reclaimed per run recorded, and the store's daily growth measured against it."
             :must-read #{seon.maintenance/collect! seon.cluster.registry/collect! seon.cluster.registry/retention-cutoff}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/health-recording-2026-09-28.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-dry-run-projects-seventy-minutes-for-a-three-minute-sweep"
             :intent "`seon.maintenance/dry-run-store!` projects `:seon.operator.collect/projected-duration-ms` as the mark plus a fixed five milliseconds per candidate (its private `projected-delete-ms-per-file`, an illustrative constant). Measured on a clone of default's 796,403-file store: 740,671 candidates swept in about 150 s, 0.2 ms per file, so the dry run projected 4,227 s against a real 763 s collection. Derive the projection from a measured sweep rate (or drop it and report only the measured mark), and record the real wall time beside it on the `collect!` receipt."
             :must-read #{seon.maintenance/collect! seon.cluster.registry/collect!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-09/store-gc.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-commit-writes-forty-index-files-and-an-eval-request-commits-at-least-once"
             :intent "Idle default has no background writer (main committed 5 times in 5 minutes); the store grows because every commit rewrites the touched leaf and path in six indexes, measured 39 files per commit (1,382 files in 5 minutes against 35 commits across 5 branches), and each eval request of every lane commits at least once. Find the per-commit file count's floor (index depth, `diff-buf-size`, history indexes) and whether a read-only or no-effect eval request needs a commit at all; the daily `seon.maintenance/collect!` only reclaims what this writes."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.store/datahike-configuration seon.maintenance/collect!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-09/store-gc.md"}}
]
